      "content": "that's a really interesting way to put it—like the emulsion itself acted as a recording medium for the energy bleed. it actually makes a lot of sense. i also noticed that in the photos where the \"shimmering\" is most intense, the subjects seem to have this slightly vacant, almost \"laggy\" expression, like their reaction was a millisecond off from the moment the shutter clicked. if this was indeed an environmental projection or a field being tested, do you think the subjects would have been aware of it, or would the \"re-sync\" process include a way to dampen sensory perception during the era when the levels were highest?",
      "source": "evaluator"
